  "notes": "D-046 / VA2B-01: this oracle run diverges to NaN (documented, not a defect of the port or of the Akantu library). With the finite-deformation material the explicit central-difference scheme is unstable at the case's time step dt = 0.8 getStableTimeStep() = 3.322158137999687e-05 (upstream patch-test choice; getStableTimeStep is a small-strain wave-speed estimate): the tangent stiffness at the affine pre-strained state (|grad u| up to 0.12) with the recorded lumped mass gives omega_max dt = 2.2042 > 2 (small strain: 1.6944; every other explicit_patch_* case <= 1.907). Rounding noise around the affine equilibrium grows by the linearised amplification factor |g| = 2.4503 per step (max |u - affine| 1.5e-16 at step 4, 1.6 at step 44); the cubic finite-deformation stress then blows it up (9.8e75 at step 48) and from step 49 to step 100 the state (u, v, a) is NaN on every free DOF (step_digests 49-100 hash NaN states). NaN quantities (count of 2,036 values): displacement (21), velocity (21), acceleration (21), internal_force (243), energy/kinetic_final (1), energy/potential (1), grad_u/_hexahedron_20 (576), piola_kirchhoff_2/_hexahedron_20 (576), cauchy/stress/_hexahedron_20 (576); stress/_hexahedron_20 (zero) and the inputs are finite. Every NaN is the platform's default quiet NaN (this aarch64 record: 0x7ff8000000000000; x86_64 produces 0xfff8000000000000), compared under the default-NaN convention D-046. Cause: probe parameters (upstream's small-strain patch-test time step applied to a genuinely finite-deformation material, a regime the upstream test never runs, UD-210). Finite FD hexahedron_20 explicit evidence: dynamic_explicit_hexahedron_20. Checks: crates/akantu-solid/tests/model_smm_fd_fixtures.rs fd_explicit_patch_hexahedron_20_diverges_from_step_49, fd_explicit_patch_time_step_against_the_stability_limit; docs/NUMERICAL_VALIDATION.md 'Default-NaN convention (D-046)'."
